---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";

import ArchitectureField from "../components/ArchitectureField.astro";
import ExpandableProjectCard from "../components/ExpandableProjectCard.astro";
import ExperienceLog from "../components/ExperienceLog.astro";
import FlowDiagram from "../components/FlowDiagram.astro";
import GovernanceChecklist from "../components/GovernanceChecklist.astro";
import IdentityBlock from "../components/IdentityBlock.astro";
import PlatformExpertise from "../components/PlatformExpertise.astro";
import PrinciplesGrid from "../components/PrinciplesGrid.astro";
import StackManifest from "../components/StackManifest.astro";
import Tabs from "../components/Tabs.astro";
---

<Layout
  title="Farnaz Zinnah — AI Systems Engineer"
  description="AI Systems Engineer working across AI infrastructure, distributed systems, adversarial machine learning, and AI governance."
>
  <main
    id="main"
    class="mx-auto max-w-6xl space-y-20 px-6 pb-28 pt-10 md:space-y-24 md:pt-14 lg:pr-12 lg:pb-20"
  >
    <!-- HERO -->
    <section
      class="relative isolate grid min-h-0 items-center gap-8 overflow-hidden py-6 sm:min-h-[55vh] sm:gap-12 sm:py-8 md:grid-cols-2"
      aria-labelledby="hero-title"
    >
      <ArchitectureField />

      <div class="relative z-10 space-y-5">
        <p
          class="font-mono text-xs uppercase tracking-[0.18em] text-accent-cyan"
        >
          AI Systems · Security · Infrastructure
        </p>

        <h1
          id="hero-title"
          class="text-4xl font-bold leading-tight tracking-tight text-text md:text-5xl"
        >
          Farnaz Zinnah
        </h1>

        <p class="max-w-md text-lg leading-8 text-text">
          I build AI systems, break them on purpose to see how they fail, and
          help decide which ones are actually safe to ship.
        </p>

        <p class="max-w-md font-mono text-sm text-secondary">
          Mostly on Azure AI Foundry and GCP.
        </p>

        <button
          type="button"
          data-scroll-target="worklab"
          data-activate-tab="work"
          class="inline-flex min-h-[44px] w-full items-center justify-center gap-2 rounded-full border border-border px-5 py-3 text-sm font-medium text-text transition-colors hover:border-accent-cyan sm:w-auto sm:py-2.5"
        >
          See selected work
          <span aria-hidden="true"> → </span>
        </button>
      </div>

      <div class="relative z-10">
        <IdentityBlock />
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- EXPERIENCE + STACK -->
    <section
      class="grid gap-10 lg:grid-cols-2"
      aria-label="Experience and technical stack"
    >
      <div id="experience" class="scroll-mt-24 space-y-3">
        <h2
          class="border-b border-border pb-2 text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight text-text md:text-3xl"
        >
          Experience
        </h2>

        <p class="text-sm text-muted">
          Mostly Con Edison so far, with school running alongside it.
        </p>

        <ExperienceLog />
      </div>

      <div id="stack" class="scroll-mt-24 space-y-3">
        <h2
          class="border-b border-border pb-2 text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight text-text md:text-3xl"
        >
          Stack
        </h2>

        <p class="text-sm text-muted">
          Not everything here makes it onto a resume bullet.
        </p>

        <StackManifest />
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- PRINCIPLES -->
    <section class="space-y-3" aria-labelledby="principles-title">
      <h2
        id="principles-title"
        class="border-b border-border pb-2 text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight text-text md:text-3xl"
      >
        How I Build
      </h2>

      <PrinciplesGrid />
    </section>

    <!-- PLATFORMS -->
    <section
      id="platforms"
      class="scroll-mt-24 space-y-5"
      aria-labelledby="platforms-title"
    >
      <div class="space-y-2">
        <h2
          id="platforms-title"
          class="border-b border-border pb-2 text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight text-text md:text-3xl"
        >
          Where I Actually Work
        </h2>

        <p class="max-w-3xl text-sm leading-6 text-muted">
          Architecture review is part of the job. Most of the hands-on cloud
          work happens across these two platforms.
        </p>
      </div>

      <PlatformExpertise />

      <p class="max-w-3xl text-sm leading-7 text-secondary">
        Production work is primarily Azure because that's the enterprise
        environment I work in. My GCP experience grew through projects where
        Vertex AI and computer-vision services fit the problem well, especially
        multimodal and drone-imagery workflows. Different constraints, different
        tools.
      </p>
    </section>

    <!-- WORK LAB -->
    <section
      id="worklab"
      class="scroll-mt-24 space-y-4"
      aria-labelledby="worklab-title"
    >
      <h2
        id="worklab-title"
        class="border-b border-border pb-2 text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight text-text md:text-3xl"
      >
        Work Lab
      </h2>

      <Tabs
        id="worklab-tabs"
        tabs={[
          {
            id: "work",
            label: "Selected Work",
          },
          {
            id: "governance",
            label: "Governance",
          },
          {
            id: "other",
            label: "Other Work",
          },
        ]}
      >
        <!-- WORK -->
        <div
          data-tab-panel="work"
          role="tabpanel"
          id="worklab-tabs-panel-work"
          aria-labelledby="worklab-tabs-tab-work"
          tabindex="0"
        >
          <p class="mb-4 text-sm text-secondary">
            Most of my day-to-day work lives in private enterprise repos. These
            are the ones I can actually show.
          </p>

          <div class="grid items-start gap-4 md:grid-cols-3">
            <ExpandableProjectCard
              size="large"
              title="Adversarial Robustness Testing"
              hook="Fooled a production image classifier down to 0.2% accuracy with changes you can't see."
              details="I wanted to know how easily a production-grade image classifier could be fooled. Turns out: very. A PGD attack dropped accuracy from 76% to 0.2%, and the trick transferred to a completely different model 90% of the time. Measured on a held-out ImageNet-1K validation subset, PGD run at ε=8/255, 20 steps. Built solo in PyTorch."
              stack={["PyTorch", "ImageNet-1K", "Security"]}
              href="https://github.com/fzinnah17/neural-network-jailbreak"
            />

            <ExpandableProjectCard
              title="Mojo vs CUDA"
              hook="Mojo's compiler kernels against a decade of CUDA optimization: closer than I expected."
              details="Mojo is still young, so I wanted to see how its compiler-generated GPU kernels stack up against CUDA's. On compute-heavy operations, Mojo won by 1.7–1.9x. On memory-bound ones, CUDA still had the edge. Co-built for HPML coursework."
              stack={["Mojo", "CUDA", "MAX Graph"]}
            />

            <ExpandableProjectCard
              title="Agentic SDLC Automation"
              platforms={["Azure"]}
              hook="Agents that sync backlogs, draft user stories, and answer questions over sprint docs."
              details="Built coordinated agents to reduce the manual overhead of sprint planning: synchronizing scope, drafting first-pass user stories, and answering backlog questions with retrieval instead of someone hunting through old tickets."
              stack={["Azure OpenAI", "RAG", "Azure DevOps", "Python"]}
            >
              <FlowDiagram
                slot="diagram"
                steps={[
                  {
                    label: "Backlog item",
                  },
                  {
                    label: "Agent drafts story",
                  },
                  {
                    label: "ADO sync",
                  },
                  {
                    label: "RAG over docs",
                  },
                ]}
              />
            </ExpandableProjectCard>

            <ExpandableProjectCard
              title="Board Materials Review Agent"
              platforms={["Azure"]}
              hook="An AI reviewer that checks a deck against structured formatting rules before manual review."
              details="Designed the architecture for a workflow that ingests a presentation, extracts slide text and formatting, checks it against structured rules with an LLM, and returns flagged inconsistencies. The generalized pattern uses short-lived storage and runtime secret resolution rather than embedding credentials in code."
              stack={["Azure OpenAI", "Blob Storage", "Key Vault", "Python"]}
            >
              <FlowDiagram
                slot="diagram"
                steps={[
                  {
                    label: "Document intake",
                  },
                  {
                    label: "Temporary storage",
                  },
                  {
                    label: "LLM rule check",
                  },
                  {
                    label: "Report + flags",
                  },
                  {
                    label: "Delivery",
                  },
                ]}
              />
            </ExpandableProjectCard>

            <ExpandableProjectCard
              title="AI Governance Agent"
              platforms={["GCP"]}
              hook="An automated first pass at the same risk questions I ask in manual review."
              details="Built a smaller automated version of the review process: takes a proposed AI or automation system description and evaluates it against risk criteria such as data sensitivity, third-party exposure, and access-control gaps before a human reviewer looks at it."
              stack={["Gemini", "Vertex AI", "Python"]}
            />
          </div>
        </div>

        <!-- GOVERNANCE -->
        <div
          data-tab-panel="governance"
          role="tabpanel"
          id="worklab-tabs-panel-governance"
          aria-labelledby="worklab-tabs-tab-governance"
          tabindex="0"
          hidden
        >
          <div class="mb-6 max-w-2xl space-y-3">
            <p
              class="font-mono text-xs uppercase tracking-[0.18em] text-accent-cyan"
            >
              Architecture &amp; Governance
            </p>

            <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold text-text">
              The other side of the table.
            </h3>

            <p class="leading-8 text-text">
              Before an AI or automation system ships, someone has to actually
              look at it and ask if it's safe. That's part of my job too. It's
              slower and less flashy than the projects above, but it's the one
              I'd probably miss most if it went away.
            </p>
          </div>

          <GovernanceChecklist />

          <p class="mt-4 text-sm leading-7 text-secondary">
            Security by default shows up in the implementation too, not just the
            review process: short-lived processing, input validation, runtime
            secret resolution, and controlled access.
          </p>
        </div>

        <!-- OTHER -->
        <div
          data-tab-panel="other"
          role="tabpanel"
          id="worklab-tabs-panel-other"
          aria-labelledby="worklab-tabs-tab-other"
          tabindex="0"
          hidden
        >
          <ul class="space-y-3 text-text">
            <li>
              <span class="font-mono text-sm text-accent-cyan">
                Infrastructure risk
              </span>

              <span
                class="ml-1 rounded border border-border px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-[10px] uppercase tracking-wide text-muted"
              >
                GCP
              </span>

              — Drone footage plus weather data, fused into a risk score for
              infrastructure inspection.
            </li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </Tabs>
    </section>

    <!-- TEACHING -->
    <section
      class="border-y border-border py-10"
      aria-labelledby="mentorship-title"
    >
      <div class="max-w-3xl space-y-4">
        <p
          class="font-mono text-xs uppercase tracking-[0.18em] text-accent-cyan"
        >
          Teaching &amp; Mentorship
        </p>

        <h2
          id="mentorship-title"
          class="text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight text-text md:text-3xl"
        >
          Didn't expect this to stick.
        </h2>

        <p class="leading-8 text-text">
          I signed up to teach data structures as a CodePath Tech Fellow mostly
          for the resume line. Ended up doing it four semesters straight, 50+
          students, 94 NPS. I still mentor for CUNY Tech Prep's AI Ethics
          program and show up for hackathons at HackMIT and Columbia DevFest
          when I can.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>
</Layout>
